ft as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/52/527eb8572b90c3d2a4449b69015a9b94f4d121b094be6629e1b92c45f2ff0eb0.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\  & =1+7+(-4) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e510a18e-355c-5760-a4ed-c27a7d87f4e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369478} {:answer/id #uuid "57708075-d434-55d2-9a8f-50cf869df4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369479} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5552ef-88b6-5aae-9816-a98a72f5bfb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369480} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e548cf-aab0-5f75-aa5e-55e9f6b0ab38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369481} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ba05f7-beee-5f04-830c-1ff34eb38cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e548cf-aab0-5f75-aa5e-55e9f6b0ab38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369481} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bd217e4-f838-5e2c-9390-01eaef7a99cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369477}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "123e0e8e-27c7-50ce-bca4-e02b7470e632" :question/math-academy-id "q-126865" :question/problem "![](images/00/00edab4b102cf705ea6c65acaa61ba524e9dba5b503167d6988b2150802d9f0b.png)\n\nSuppose that $\\mathbf{F}$ is a vector field on ${\\mathbb{R}}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=7,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=-9,\\hspace{2em}{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ is oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/be/be04b9b505d71a99f7333ca9e9e9755c78453421f5aaf197306cbc5f2ca8df63.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientation of the inner curve ${C}_{3}$ is opposite that of ${C}_{3}$ as stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\  & =7+(-9)-1 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a1d2c6b-2930-525d-8d87-b98d293ac862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/m