the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/85/85a8ea287d2cb8e3b70e332ac444a9e06262fef35369d1bad1f24ea5c9d31687.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the outer and inner curves are opposite those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\  & =-6-2-(-10) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b2f076-3c1b-5b41-b54d-acbf22c85f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369492} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf840d4-a3b7-5a1f-8ab9-000eaa11d729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369493} {:answer/id #uuid "544f331d-d37a-57d2-a8ec-3849a346d73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369494} {:answer/id #uuid "7953c459-d75a-5d7a-a051-42cf152ae33e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369495} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7aedd6-9474-596f-83c6-b28c824b5114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7953c459-d75a-5d7a-a051-42cf152ae33e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369495} :answer-field/id #uuid "998a54d8-ef67-567f-aff6-05f6543