unterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/b2/b20b2b911c2a417c26fa951d9b28efa296c265df25e9d06b635ef4846267b93b.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\  & =16+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "576b4a58-c183-5275-bda2-05fe1ba9c5fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{59}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543815} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff2ff02-02b1-5751-b12a-7e9ef64a27e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{97}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543820} {:answer/id #uuid "857a4020-99d9-5010-bea5-959744696366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{59}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543821} {:answer/id #uuid "a3810977-df2d-5104-b3e0-f2a4d0401184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543827} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c3520-3e82-5867-91f7-0be0499e3c49" :answer/type {:db/id