 that the positive orientations of the inner curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are opposite to those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{25}{3}\\right)-\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{13}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-50)-32-39}{6} \\\\  & =- \\frac{121}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fa1ed4-4d14-540d-97de-17e4ea742baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543807} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed577c8-30fd-548a-b930-79b44fab958d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{91}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543810} {:answer/id #uuid "58497438-3492-546e-943f-9a79c035517d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543816} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b06cad-9359-531f-99db-dcc71b377046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543829} {:answer/id #uuid "bd10c665-5dc5-55ab-9e3d-c447f60443ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{29}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58497438-3492-546e-943f-9a79c035517d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543816} :answer-field/id #uuid "95746fd1-feb5-5b16-a7b6-2ceb1c8e2219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543823}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8e9f007-9cb8-5437-b13d-dccd4da1a757" :question/problem "![](images/12/1253965689fbeb233ca3eda553cca8ea8bced9feb81ebc6565c9b65782066b47.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{17}{2},\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=- \\frac{19}{3},\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=- \\frac{1}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{3}$ is oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/ca/cad0f92fdd888243562619b410a200ca040ca43f83bfd15fb124c8a8ecae4df6.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientation of the inner curve ${C}_{2}$ is opposite that of ${C}_{2}$ as stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{2}-\\left(- \\frac{19}{3}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{1}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{51-(-38)+(-2)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0015fc8-88b5-5637-806e-0694134e0bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543826} {:answer/id #uuid "bbea5b3d-93cf-5bdb-b3b9-dc8d398f6a5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543830} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1bfe2-984f-576e-a3ec-0532fcc4e3e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{47}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543833} {:answer/id #uuid "e971687d-bfd0-50d9-822f-623b570efa14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{89}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543835} {:answer/id #uuid "fa61e5ce-3036-5c2e-9dab-860447db6fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1bfe2-984f-576e-a3ec-0532fcc4e3e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{47}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543833} :answer-field/id #uuid "99656766-dc06-5ada-8132-f7b86b695e08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543824}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f0468836-7eb8-505a-98df-3234db3c120b" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1f308d1a3ecf3bd0090e22c4f70389311db4db3ff06f7038db0cf7770a8837c7.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=- \\frac{7}{2},\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=- \\frac{14}{3},\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{20}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are oriented clockwise and ${C}_{3}$ is oriented counterclockwise, calculate the value of $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/2b/2bed1b367cd101e0e90674c619ad87da8c90744df570eeea4d9b0333ccee0de1.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the outer curve ${C}_{1}$ and the inner curve ${C}_{3}$ are opposite those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{14}{3}\\right)-\\frac{20}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-21)+(-28)-40}{6} \\\\  & =- \\frac{47}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circulation of a Vector Field Over a Region Containing Holes"}]}
